    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d85">

                <pb facs="0205" n="89" sameAs="frus:frus1914/pg89"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">File No. 493.00/1.</note>
                <head>
                    <hi rendition="#italic">The Secretary of State to Minister Reinsch.</hi>
                </head>
                <opener>
                    <seg rendition="#float-left">No. 38.]</seg>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right">
                        <placeName>
                            <hi rendition="#small-caps">Department of State</hi>, <lb/>
                            <hi rendition="#italic">Washington</hi></placeName>, <date
                            calendar="gregorian" when="1914-02-04">
                            <hi rendition="#italic">February 4, 1914</hi></date>.</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>
                    <hi rendition="#small-caps">Sir</hi>: The Department is in receipt of your
                    dispatch No. 57 of January 2, 1914, enclosing correspondence exchanged with the
                    Consul General at Hankow relative to claims against China growing out of the
                    revolution of 1911–1912. Your dispatch and its enclosures have been read with
                    interest.</p>
                <p>With respect to the proposal to limit the grounds for claims against China, you
                    are authorized to endeavor to induce the Diplomatic Body to consent to such
                    limitations as will prevent injustice to the Chinese Government, bearing in mind
                    in this connection the Department’s telegram of December 20, on this
                        subject.<anchor n="34" xml:id="d85-f1"/>
                </p>
                <p>I am [etc.]</p>
                <closer>For the Secretary of State: <lb/>
                    <signed>
                        <hi rendition="#small-caps">J. W. Folk</hi></signed>.</closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
